menu "Free Harvest Adapter"

config HR_AP_SSID
    string "Setup access-point SSID"
    default "HR-Adapter-Setup"
    help
        SSID broadcast when no WiFi credentials are stored (or the stored
        network can't be joined). Connect to it to reach the setup page.

config HR_AP_PASSWORD
    string "Setup access-point password (blank = open)"
    default ""
    help
        Password for the setup AP. Leave blank for an open network. If set,
        must be at least 8 characters (WPA2 requirement).

config HR_ACK_PAYLOAD
    string "GOTIT ack payload (UNVERIFIED)"
    default "ESP32ADAPTER"
    help
        Value sent in the GOTIT acknowledgement. The genuine adapter's
        payload is not yet known - capture it with a USB sniffer and set it
        here (or leave for later; the decoding UI works regardless).

config HR_HTTP_LOG_TO_UART
    bool "Also echo received frames to the UART console"
    default y

config HR_LOG_RING_KB
    int "In-app log ring (/api/log) size, KB"
    range 4 128
    default 32
    help
        Static DRAM reserved for the in-app copy of the ESP-IDF log that
        /api/log serves. Lines are stored packed (a line costs its own
        length plus two bytes), so 32 KB keeps roughly 500 lines of the
        ~65-character average - a boot, the handshake and several minutes
        of a busy link. Boards without PSRAM that carry other RAM users can
        turn this down; the ring only ever drops its oldest lines.

config HR_CAPTURE_RAW
    bool "Capture log: keep every frame verbatim (no repeat collapsing)"
    default n
    help
        By default consecutive identical frames (an idle dryer's REQINFO
        every 10 s) are collapsed into one "repeat ... xN" summary line to
        save flash. Enable this when recording traffic for protocol work,
        where the exact cadence of every frame matters more than space.
        On a 16 MB board the 11.9 MB capture partition holds several days
        of raw traffic even so.

endmenu
